// P41W (portsim/sim/gfx_uvwide.h; log/roadmap/P41/PORT_WIDE_BRIEF.md, log/roadmap/P41/portwide/notes.md): the wide front-end
// backdrops (module gfx_uvwide). The screens are uivec_wide_<screen>.inc, generated by re/tools/uivec/port_export.py --wide; every
// formula is re/tools/uivec/sdf.py's and wide.py's (gfx_uivec_eval.h), so a render equals wide.render of the same scene
// (port/test/test_p41_uivec.py).
//
// Speed: the target is cut into 32 x 32 tiles; every op's item, blob or picture is binned into the tiles its pixel box touches (its
// box as sdf.render computes it), and the tiles are painted on the machine's threads, each tile from its own list in paint order
// (a tile's pixels depend only on the entries over it, so tiles are independent). The leading ground ops are painted at no more
// than kUwGroundScaleMax target pixels per frame unit on a grid and upsampled bilinearly (exact below it).
#include "portsim/sim/gfx_uvwide.h"

